{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch23sute2P64MmBx7wm5u", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FL3pebgWA2HciyiFhmheGA", "name": "mcp__device__sign_off", "input": {"verdict": "PASS", "confidence": 0.45, "notes": "Not a clean pass. One confirmed bug is logged: with Subtasks = \"My order\", flipping the global Sorting direction does not reverse the nested subtasks under \"Pack for trip\" (Print tickets stays above Charge phone in both Ascending and Descending). This is the build's \"nested items in manual mode follow the global direction\" change, so it needs a fix before release.\n\nChecked and looked correct: sort sheet reflects saved list prefs after reopening and across rotation; Sorting picker (By title) reorders groups; subtask sort by title (Asc/Desc) reverses; repeat picker shows the current rule; Custom recurrence loads \"every 2 weeks\", \"every 1 month\", \"every 1 day / after 1 occurrence\" and \"every 1 hour\"; completing Final dose moves it to Completed and Undo restores it; completing Pay rent (monthly) reschedules to Jan 4, 2027; Water plants (hourly) reschedules to 11 AM; Weekly review (2 weeks) reschedules to Dec 28; subtask completion updates the parent count and Undo restores it; rotation in the editor and the list keeps state.\n\nNot reproduced: a report that \"Repeats on\" showed no weekday for the weekly task was reported as not reproducible, so I did not count it as a bug. Not covered: changing repeat values on a saved task, the 0/boundary inputs for the recurrence count, Read docs link handling, the Grouping option, and sorting by priority/start date/last modified/smart sort."}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2392, "cache_read_input_tokens": 185015, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2392}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a4e81c7d-cad5-4371-8b19-91602191b671", "uuid": "f8715d69-c63b-40d2-9ccf-5371f5018e00", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T02:42:45.884Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch23sud1jYGQwN5jMWsXD", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01FL3pebgWA2HciyiFhmheGA": {"verdict": "PASS", "confidence": 0.45, "notes": "Not a clean pass. One confirmed bug is logged: with Subtasks = \"My order\", flipping the global Sorting direction does not reverse the nested subtasks under \"Pack for trip\" (Print tickets stays above Charge phone in both Ascending and Descending). This is the build's \"nested items in manual mode follow the global direction\" change, so it needs a fix before release.\n\nChecked and looked correct: sort sheet reflects saved list prefs after reopening and across rotation; Sorting picker (By title) reorders groups; subtask sort by title (Asc/Desc) reverses; repeat picker shows the current rule; Custom recurrence loads \"every 2 weeks\", \"every 1 month\", \"every 1 day / after 1 occurrence\" and \"every 1 hour\"; completing Final dose moves it to Completed and Undo restores it; completing Pay rent (monthly) reschedules to Jan 4, 2027; Water plants (hourly) reschedules to 11 AM; Weekly review (2 weeks) reschedules to Dec 28; subtask completion updates the parent count and Undo restores it; rotation in the editor and the list keeps state.\n\nNot reproduced: a report that \"Repeats on\" showed no weekday for the weekly task was reported as not reproducible, so I did not count it as a bug. Not covered: changing repeat values on a saved task, the 0/boundary inputs for the recurrence count, Read docs link handling, the Grouping option, and sorting by priority/start date/last modified/smart sort."}}, "tool_use_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01FL3pebgWA2HciyiFhmheGA",